format session-log-v1
stamp 20260813.201515
editor Zed + Claude Agent
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host Ubuntu 26.04 LTS GNOME Wayland (Framework 16 AMD) — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title HUNK46 — the touch session: finger down · move · up become a live cursor
prompt Continue the autonomous loop — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop only at custody gates.
think HUNK40–45 grew the touch-scroll journey in six clean pieces, each called separately. The capstone crux is the integration face a real device event loop actually calls — one object a touchscreen hands finger_down, a stream of finger_move, then finger_up, ticking between frames. That driver is the durable public face of the whole stack.
think Designed a small three-phase state machine (idle · dragging · flinging): finger_down enters dragging and cancels any coast (grab-to-stop); finger_move drags the cursor by the pixel delta since the last position (HUNK44) and remembers it as the live velocity; finger_up seeds a fling from that velocity (HUNK45) or returns idle if the finger was at rest; tick/settle step the coast. Every motion routes through the proven pieces, so the session adds no arithmetic and no new clamp — only the phase transitions and grab-to-stop.
think Safety: deltas taken in i64 and clamped to i32 so a wild finger jump never wraps; the fling seed clamped into HUNK45's velocity cap so finger_up never fails; friction and cell height validated once at open (catch unreachable at finger_up is honest — both preconditions already hold).
obs One value model (a phase enum, three counts, two owned sub-structs), refusals only BadCellHeight/BadFriction at open, no storage, no render, no timer — a caller ticks it per frame. Velocity smoothing and rubber-band overscroll are named horizons.
obs Built GREEN first try; no shadowing red this time. Split every compound assert by hand; TAME bans clean, width exit 0. The GREEN print line carries no apostrophe, so the witness grep passed first build (the ladder's reflexive fix held).
obs The selftest drives whole gestures, not method calls in isolation: a pure drag (still finger before release → no fling), a flick (moving finger → coasts to the bottom-pinned offset), grab-to-stop (finger_down mid-coast freezes the cursor where caught), a hard flick (clamped, no overshoot) — so a phase-transition bug is caught by the observable cursor behaviour.
loom witness=hunk_touch_scroll_witness cell_px=10 viewport=2x5 max_offset=3 friction=3/4 gestures=drag,flick,grab_to_stop,hard_flick
file pond/apps/preset_touch_scroll.rye HUNK46 — TouchScroll routes finger_down/move/up and per-frame tick through HUNK44 drag + HUNK45 fling; grab-to-stop cancels a coast.
file tools/hunk_touch_scroll_witness.rish proves the driver on metal — pure-drag no fling, flick that coasts, grab-to-stop, inherited clamp, open-time refusals.
file active-designing/20260813-201244_hunk-touch-session-exploration.md self-approved design read.
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md git nib refreshed in this same work commit.
recommend keep-going — the touch-scroll journey (HUNK40 cursor · 41 bar · 42 view · 43 input · 44 drag · 45 fling · 46 session) now stands whole end to end; HUNK47 could pivot to a fresh Season-A / double-seat journey (the McMaster-Carr served marketplace's module-assembly ruling is held for Keaton), add rubber-band overscroll or velocity smoothing, or wire the touch session onto the painted HUNK42 scroll view.
